            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of gem-Difluoroallylboronates via FeCl2-Catalyzed Boration/β-Fluorine Elimination of Trifluoromethyl Alkenes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>946-949</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b00168</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first ferrous chloride catalyzed boration/β-fluorine elimination of trifluoromethyl alkenes is described. Thus, a full range of gem-difluoroallylboronates were obtained in high yield under mild conditions. As an important fluorinated building block, gem-difluoroallylboronate can be readily converted into diverse difluoro-substituted species.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
